    "body": "I suppose. If you define `async getData` that takes a signal. And internally it uses `async getDataInternal` that also takes a signal. It could pass the outer signal to `getDataInternal` and await `getDataInternal` to see if it gets an AbortError or some kind of success and based on that decide to return or throw for `getData`. It's a choice of course whether it wants to wait for `getDataInternal`, but there's nothing we can really do about that I think.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
